# PM Wiki Dashboard — Obsidian Bases

This file configures four live views using Obsidian Bases.
Each view surfaces a different health signal across the vault.

> To activate: open this file in Obsidian and enable the Bases plugin.

---

## View 1: Recent (last 7 days)

Filter: `date_modified >= today - 7`
Sort: `date_modified DESC`
Columns: title, type, status, tldr, confidence

Use to: track what changed this week, catch unreviewed recent additions.

---

## View 2: Low confidence

Filter: `confidence = "low" OR confidence = "uncertain"`
Sort: `type ASC, date_modified ASC`
Columns: title, type, confidence, explored, tldr

Use to: find pages that need more evidence or PM review before relying on them.

---

## View 3: Unexplored

Filter: `explored = false`
Sort: `date_modified ASC` (oldest first)
Columns: title, type, status, confidence, tldr

Use to: find pages the LLM created that the PM hasn't personally validated yet.

---

## View 4: Stale data

Filter: `type = "data" AND status = "active"`
Sort: `date_modified ASC`
Columns: title, tldr, confidence

Use to: identify data insights that may have passed their freshness window.
Cross-check against the `Freshness` field in each page body.

---

*Requires Obsidian Bases plugin (community plugin).*
*All views are read-only — edit pages directly in Obsidian.*
